## Phase 3, round 4

October 19, 2026, `claude/premium-phase-1` at 8c4264c. Read only: nothing submitted, saved, withdrawn or confirmed; failure states were answered in my own browser only. One browser process at a time.

The preview on port 51349 crashed at about 15:25 (a Turbopack panic in `next.log`, after DB statement timeouts had already sent Home a 500 on every load). Everything that hit the old port was re-run on the restarted preview at `http://127.0.0.1:60059`. Only the 51349 results that loaded cleanly are kept; they agree with the re-runs.

Evidence: `P3R4` = `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-josek0514-Desktop-NEVORA-UI-READINESS/8c7acfe8-4195-49cb-a26a-ba2ac9ec5c59/scratchpad/phase7/widths/p3r4/` (`crops/`, `shots/`, `data/*.jsonl`). Scripts: `sweep.mjs` (one load per page, then 100/125/150/200% on that page), `sheet.mjs` (More sheet), `fail.mjs` (500 and 401 on `/api/`), `skel.mjs` (placeholder frames on a direct load) and `js/`. Source: `.claude/worktrees/premium-phase-1`.

### Verdict

**Not zero: 8 defects open in widths, roles and consistency (0 P0, 2 P1, 6 P2).** Ten of the fifteen IDs are closed: P3-WR-01 to 06, 08, 09, 10 and 15. Five are partly fixed and stay open: P3-WR-07, 11, 12, 13 and 14. There are three new defects, all at large text. Two are P1:
- The My schedule week list's day column collides with the shift times (P3-WR-16).
- My time's entry total runs into the clock time and off the card (P3-WR-17).

The third is P2: the new `keepWhole` keeps a whole date heading on one line, so it gets cut at 200% (P3-WR-18). Nothing scrolls sideways on any page, width, text size or account measured.

### Status of P3-WR-01 to P3-WR-15

| ID | Status | Measurement now |
|---|---|---|
| P3-WR-01 | **Fixed** | Week strip is one row at 320, 360, 390, 430 and 844×390 (Chromium and WebKit). At 360, 390 and 430 all 7 days fit (44 / 45 / 51px). At 320 it scrolls (328 in 288) with the right fade. |
| P3-WR-02 | **Fixed** | Holds for AUDIT-E and AUDIT-LEAD at 390: title 17/22/500, time 15/20, "Action required" a 28px kit pill (#FDF1DC), Refresh a quiet 44px control, head 17/22/600. |
| P3-WR-03 | **Fixed** | Minimum gap between tab labels: 19 / 28.9 / 34.9 / 26.2 / 109px at 320 / 360 / 390 / 430 / landscape. At 125–200% it's 11.2 / 22 / 28.6 / 17.4 / 100.2px. No overlap. |
| P3-WR-04 | **Fixed** | No switch overlaps a day name (overlap 0 on every row) at 320, 360, 390 and landscape, 100–200%, for AUDIT-E and AUDIT-LEAD. Every switch ends at the row edge. |
| P3-WR-05 | **Fixed** | Holds. The Lead now gets the Employee's controls (see 09). |
| P3-WR-06 | **Fixed** | Days now grow with text: 44 / 55 / 66 / 88px at 100 / 125 / 150 / 200%. The strip scrolls (636 in 288 at 320/200%) and no labels in the strip overlap. WebKit agrees. |
| P3-WR-07 | **Open (P2)** | 320 is now right: all seven rows stack at 100–200%. Wider phones still mix the two layouts in one list:<br>**360 at 150%:** only Wednesday stacks (switch 40px under the name); the other six are inline.<br>**360 at 200%:** six rows stack, Friday stays inline.<br>**390 at 200%:** Wed, Thu and Sat stack; Mon, Tue, Fri and Sun stay inline.<br>(`data/main.jsonl`, `avail.js`.) The fix at `portal-premium.css:1393` (`@container (max-width: 15.5rem)`) only matches at 320. In Chromium the `rem` in that query doesn't follow the page's text size, so it never matches at 360+ even at 200%. **Fix:** put the threshold in `em` against a container that scales with the text (`.av-day-list { font-size: 1rem }` with `@container (max-width: 15.5em)`), or stack every row whenever the longest name and the switch can't share a line (for example, `@container (max-width: 22em)`). Check in WebKit too. |
| P3-WR-08 | **Fixed** | On every row at 320, 360 and 390, 100–200% (AUDIT-E 5 rows, AUDIT-LEAD 1), the pill sits under the dates at x=36 (`flex-direction: column`) and each timeline event starts its own line. |
